module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.emitter_index_keyed_on_a_type_leaf_takes_the_last_declarer

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data emitter_index_keyed_on_a_type_leaf_takes_the_last_declarer: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "emitter_index_keyed_on_a_type_leaf_takes_the_last_declarer" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "an emitter index keyed on a type's leaf takes the last declarer: the Rust emitter builds its per-closure facts about type declarations into maps keyed on the declared LEAF NAME, folded over every module with map_insert, so when two modules of one closure declare the same leaf the map holds ONE row -- whichever was folded last -- and every reader of either declaration is answered with that row. INVALID STATE: a declaration emitted from another declaration's facts. Nothing refuses: the lookup is Present, the row is well-formed, and it is about a different type.",

    "HARM, IN TWO GRADES. Where the foreign fact contradicts the Rust the declaration needs, rustc refuses and the closure does not build -- loud, but located at the emitted field, not at the collision. Where the foreign fact is merely DIFFERENT -- a sharing decision, a variant-to-enum owner, a field's access style, a derive set that still compiles -- the emitted program builds and behaves as the other declaration's facts dictate, which is the silent grade and the reason this is a row and not a build fix.",

    "SPECIMEN, the native approval broker closure (entry dag/gunbc/auth/approval_broker_serve.dag, lane 2A of the native-broker program, main fd30a502): std.access declares AccessRequest<S, A, O, C, E> and gunbc.auth.access_request declares AccessRequest<Subject>. v1.compiler.infer_emit_info add_emit_item_summary inserted both under `AccessRequest`; v1.compiler.trait_derive_emit v1_clone_bounded_type_params therefore held the one-element set Subject for that key, v1_item_clone_bounded_param_names filtered std.access's own [S, A, O, C, E] against it and found none, and std_access.rs printed `pub struct AccessRequest<S, A, O, C, E>` over fields naming AccessContext<C: Clone> and AccessEvidence<E: Clone>: ten rustc errors (E0277, E0369). The paired control is the same emitter over dag/std/authorization_profile.dag, whose closure has one AccessRequest and prints all five bounds.",

    "WHAT IS CLOSED AND WHAT IS NOT. The trait-derive family is re-keyed on the declaration -- v1.compiler.infer_emit_info TypeDeclIndex (EmitGraphInfo.type_decl_items), and with it clone_bounded_type_params, clone_impl_required_type_params and map_key_required_type_names -- under the item registry's own identity (v1.std.core callable_identity over owner module and declared name), and a reference reaches a row through resolve_type_decl_routed, whose spelling arm REFUSES a leaf two modules declare. RE-KEYED IN A SECOND CUT: type_summaries is a TypeSummaryIndex keyed by the same declaration identity (variant-payload rows under `<identity>::<Variant>`), and variant_to_enum maps each variant to its owner's identity, so a second same-leaf declaration no longer replaces the first's summary for readers in other modules (the unit row same_leaf_type_elsewhere_leaves_other_modules_emission_unchanged). Readers that hold only a NAME read it through type_summary_decided, which answers no summary for a leaf two declarations own; that residue ends when TypeSummary's field_type_map and field_import_surface_names store identities. THIRD CUT, HONEST BOUNDARY: v1.compiler.emit_rust build_shared_types / maybe_mark_shared_type INSERT by TypeSummary.key (type_decl_identity), and a unique-owner Pascal leaf is a dual key, not a last-write-wins collapse. is_type_constant still looks up that key in identity_keyed_recursive_type_set, which copies EVERY identity whose leaf sits in EmitGraphInfo.recursive_type_set. That set is still leaf-keyed last-write-wins. So if one module's Foo is recursive and another's is not, both identities are marked recursive, the non-recursive Foo cannot be a type constant, and it is shared. Sharing is therefore keyed by declaration only where the name is not in the recursive set; the census already answers SharingUndeterminedByDeclaration for that case (v1.tests.claim.shared_type_leaf_collision_census). STILL LEAF-KEYED, LAST WRITE WINS, on v1.compiler.infer_emit_info EmitGraphInfo: fn_decl_items, recursive_type_set, fielded_variants, positional_payload_variants, and this sharing residual. data_variant_wire_spellings is keyed on the coproduct's leaf too but stores DataVariantSpellingRefused when two declarers disagree, so it fails closed; ownership_index and read_only_params_index are module-qualified and are not members.",

    "A DECLARED MIDDLE STATE INSIDE THE CLOSED PART: kernel spellings. A kernel spelling (std.types is_kernel_type) is a reference resolve deliberately leaves unstamped, and the corpus also declares some of those leaves in two modules: v2.std.text and v2.std.node String, std.integer and v2.std.integer Int. Bool was a third until v2.std.logic Bool was retired; the arm is about any kernel-spelled leaf with two declarers, not about a fixed list. For such a reference the routed resolution answers TypeDeclKernelSpellingUndecided: it does NOT refuse, it derives no Clone or Ord bound from either declaration, and it carries a map-key requirement to EVERY declarer of the leaf, which is what the leaf-keyed set did. So for these leaves the emitted derives are unchanged by the re-keying and the question of which declaration a kernel-spelled position denotes is still open. Each occurrence is one row of v1.tests.claim.carrier_realization_census (emitter_decl_route). TRIGGER, at capability grain: resolve identifies a kernel-spelled reference -- as the kernel type or as the corpus declaration its scope binds -- at every type position the emitter reads; the owner is the text-boundary identity work (gunbc.rung_drop text_boundary_identity_wall), not the emitter. One stamped position does not retire the arm.",

    "RUNG: for the trait-derive family, mechanically preventable -- gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls (two ControlSlot declarations of different arity in one closure, emitted, built and run) and the unit row same_leaf_type_declarations_emit_their_own_bounds are the discriminating red and the positive control. For the indexes still leaf-keyed, including sharing when the name is in recursive_type_set, mitigatable at best: the collision is observed only when rustc happens to refuse the foreign fact. ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally impossible -- an index keyed on the declaration has no row two declarations can share. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: every EmitGraphInfo index that answers a question about a type declaration is keyed on the declaration's identity and reached from a reference through the one routed resolution, so that adding a same-leaf declaration to any module of a closure cannot change what is emitted for an existing one. Re-keying one more map is not that capability; the trigger is the set.",

    "OCCURRENCE 2026-10-22, the shared-type set (gunbc#13936, replacing closed #14816): std.bit.Word64 { items: Rc<Vec<..>> } was emitted with derive(Copy), E0204, because a second unrelated std.machine_word.Word64 { hi: Int, lo: Int } entered the same closure (effect_pair_census -> v2.compiler.effect_demand -> v2.workflow.floor_discovery -> extdeps.git.object_store -> std.encoding -> std.machine_word) and the Copy decision was keyed on the bare name. Found by the B0 branch emitting source_root_eval. The set is now keyed on TypeSummary.key, the declaration identity, and a position whose reference cannot be resolved to one identity answers SharedLayerRefuse, which the renderers emit as a compile_error! arm.",

    "READERS OF THE SHARED SET, the census of what asks the sharing question through shared_layer_of_type_expr: type-position wrap and deref, struct field types, function signatures, match scrutinee, spread and clone, let and lambda annotations, fold accumulators, data and constructor definitions, and the needs-box answer. A typed pre-pass over the same positions was built and DELETED in the same change: no real source reaches it, because resolve stamps references and the interim unstamped producer, a union body member, is a variant declaration rather than a type reference (see accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target, the E0428 receipt), so its RED could not be authored and it would have been a decoration. The render-time compile_error! arms stay as the declared residue (gunbc.rung_drop emitter_shared_layer_refusal_floor_is_render_time).",

    "DISAGREEING LEAF PAIRS measured in the corpus: NonNegativeInt and PositiveInt, OccurrenceBinding, SourceSpan are declared in two modules with different layers, so a bare-leaf reference to them refuses rather than guessing. OccurrenceId does NOT collide.",

    "NEXT WALL after this repair: native-materialization-store-closure fails rustc E0282 at std_list.rs:44:37, an inference-grounding defect unrelated to the shared set. RESIDUAL: the recursive_type_set index is still leaf-keyed and stays declared.",

    "RUNG for the shared set: mechanically preventable. The census gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:shared-type-leaf-collision-census holds the discriminating fixtures (red_entry two same-leaf types accepted with different sharing, recursive fixtures undetermined, green accepted). The render-time refuse arms have no authored RED: no source fixture reaches one. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: every type position carries a resolve stamp (emitter_decl_route at zero in v1.tests.claim.carrier_realization_census), which deletes the arms and the interim RouteLeafSpelling producer.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_emit_info", decl_name: "TypeDeclIndex"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_emit_info", decl_name: "resolve_type_decl_routed"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_emit_info", decl_name: "EmitGraphInfo"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls", decl_name: "same_leaf_declaration_cases"),
  ],
}
